ojectionPlan` test failed. Strict duplicate framing plants were killed. |\n12|| Operation ordering and DAG | **broken** F2 | Four-operation equal-sequence dependency plant survived the existing package suite, then a public `BuildProjectionPlan` test failed. Independent two-operation equal-edge plant was killed. |\n13|| Resource and entry nullability | **broken** F3 | A blob with two missing blob-only members bypassed the branch check and panicked in `BuildProjectedObjectManifest`; the existing package suite stayed green, while the new public-entry test failed. Resource blob-null plant was killed. |\n14|| Sorted arrays, scalar bounds, plan constants, policies, vocabulary | **held** | Shipped harness rerun twice; own key-bound-plus-one and second-value constant plants killed. The one-million-mapping upper boundary was not attacked at a public entry because a suitable fixture was missing; the submitted edge test reaches only the factored helper. |\n15|| Omit-self JCS identities | **held** | Independent Python JCS + SHA-256 recomputation matched both emitted fixture IDs. |\n16|| Importer outcomes and composition | **held** | Base and candidate tests passed for six reused owner packages; all 171 files in those packages are byte-identical, so no class moved in their entries. The producer's table is package-level rather than the requested `(package, entry, input)` grid. |\n17|| Exact-tree hygiene | **broken** F4 | `git diff --check BASE CANDIDATE` exits 2 on a new blank line at EOF in the mutant harness. The producer's plain `git diff --check` did not inspect its untracked files. |\n18|\n19|## Findings\n20|\n21|```verdict-findings\n22|{\n23|  \"findings\": [\n24|    {\n25|      \"id\": \"member-case-variant-uncounted\",\n26|      \"row\": \"Closed member sets and strict frame\",\n27|      \"invariant\": \"The committed member census must derive all members from Go types and kill a narrowing that accepts a miscased required member through DecodeProjectionPlan.\",\n28|      \"mechanism\": \"internal/cloneplan/members_test.go:87 hand-lists the member census; TestMemberCensusMiscased at line 280 tries only strings.ToUpper. Reflection in utf8_reflection_test.go covers only string-valued UTF-8 fields. A Titlecase Strategy normalization at decodeStrictObject survives the existing suite.\",\n29|      \"reproductions\": [\n30|        {\n31|          \"test_file\": \"review_casefold_test.go\",\n32|          \"command\": \"go test -count=1 -run '^TestReviewTitlecaseRefusal$' ./internal/cloneplan on exact candidate: exit 0\",\n33|          \"expected_failure\": \"on casefold-plant.patch applied to candidate: expected test failure, exit 1, Titlecase member admitted; logs casefold-candidate.log and casefold-casefold.log\",\n34|          \"pinned_blobs\": [\n35|            \"sha256:c17ab7089cc1f2cc22c9290fb39845fe5d357d26e8044551a9e120ed32984ca2\",\n36|            \"sha256:d08ed7f25035f5f6c705416e353568db838ac17c7fd97b843afc8cb3258bdc93\"\n37|          ]\n38|        },\n39|        {\n40|          \"test_file\": \"go test -count=1 ./internal/cloneplan on the casefold mutant without the review test: exit 0\",\n41|          \"command\": \"log casefold-existing-suite.log\",\n42|          \"expected_failure\": \"go test -count=1 ./internal/cloneplan on the casefold mutant without the review test: exit 0; log casefold-existing-suite.log\",\n43|          \"pinned_blobs\": [\n44|            \"sha256:c17ab7089cc1f2cc22c9290fb39845fe5d357d26e8044551a9e120ed32984ca2\",\n45|            \"sha256:d08ed7f25035f5f6c705416e353568db838ac17c7fd97b843afc8cb3258bdc93\"\n46|          ]\n47|        },\n48|        {\n49|          \"test_file\": \"coverage_audit.py <exact candidate copy>: expected exit 1 for non-reflection-derived member census\",\n50|          \"command\": \"log coverage-audit.log\",\n51|          \"expected_failure\": \"coverage_audit.py <exact candidate copy>: expected exit 1 for non-reflection-derived member census; log coverage-audit.log\",\n52|          \"pinned_blobs\": [\n53|            \"sha256:c17ab7089cc1f2cc22c9290fb39845fe5d357d26e8044551a9e120ed32984ca2\",\n54|            \"sha256:d08ed7f25035f5f6c705416e353568db838ac17c7fd97b843afc8cb3258bdc93\"\n55|          ]\n56|        }\n57|      ],\n58|      \"severity\": \"bypass\",\n59|      \"repeat-of\": \"none\"\n60|    },\n61|    {\n62|      \"id\": \"dag-large-invalid-uncounted\",\n63|      \"row\": \"Operation ordering and DAG\",\n64|      \"invariant\": \"Every dependency graph through five operations is classified against the independent oracle, including invalid four- and five-operation graphs.\",\n65|      \"mechanism\": \"internal/cloneplan/dag_test.go:108 enumerates all graphs only through three operations; lines 144+ enumerate only valid four- and five-operation graphs. The four-operation self-edge exception in dagfour-plant.patch survives the existing suite.\",\n66|      \"reproductions\": [\n67|        {\n68|          \"test_file\": \"review_dagfour_test.go\",\n69|          \"command\": \"go test -count=1 -run '^TestReviewFourNodeSelfEdgeRefusal$' ./internal/cloneplan on exact candidate: exit 0\",\n70|          \"expected_failure\": \"on dagfour-plant.patch: expected test failure, exit 1, four-node self edge admitted; logs dagfour-candidate.log and dagfour-dagfour.log\",\n71|          \"pinned_blobs\": [\n72|            \"sha256:8f11ee28b8a2f685a9f6b36bb8c7c6bab6a0f4f13a4a9592c46f3dcdecca43f3\",\n73|            \"sha256:d6a6f394a7cf7020c755ed6a424b92b1b5d4dd31fc54703cf03fc9b71553dcd0\"\n74|          ]\n75|        },\n76|        {\n77|          \"test_file\": \"go test -count=1 ./internal/cloneplan on the dagfour mutant without the review test: exit 0\",\n78|          \"command\": \"log dagfour-existing-suite.log\",\n79|          \"expected_failure\": \"go test -count=1 ./internal/cloneplan on the dagfour mutant without the review test: exit 0; log dagfour-existing-suite.log\",\n80|          \"pinned_blobs\": [\n81|            \"sha256:8f11ee28b8a2f685a9f6b36bb8c7c6bab6a0f4f13a4a9592c46f3dcdecca43f3\",\n82|            \"sha256:d6a6f394a7cf7020c755ed6a424b92b1b5d4dd31fc54703cf03fc9b71553dcd0\"\n83|          ]\n84|        },\n85|        {\n86|          \"test_file\": \"coverage_audit.py <exact candidate copy>: expected exit 1 for no all-graph sweep through five operations\",\n87|          \"command\": \"log coverage-audit.log\",\n88|          \"expected_failure\": \"coverage_audit.py <exact candidate copy>: expected exit 1 for no all-graph sweep through five operations; log coverage-audit.log\",\n89|          \"pinned_blobs\": [\n90|            \"sha256:8f11ee28b8a2f685a9f6b36bb8c7c6bab6a0f4f13a4a9592c46f3dcdecca43f3\",\n91|            \"sha256:d6a6f394a7cf7020c755ed6a424b92b1b5d4dd31fc54703cf03fc9b71553dcd0\"\n92|          ]\n93|        }\n94|      ],\n95|      \"severity\": \"bypass\",\n96|      \"repeat-of\": \"none\"\n97|    },\n98|    {\n99|      \"id\": \"entry-presence-combinations-uncounted\",\n100|      \"row\": \"Resource and entry nullability\",\n101|      \"invariant\": \"The blob/directory kind × each blob-only field-presence combination must be checked through both manifest entries and refuse structurally.\",\n102|      \"mechanism\": \"internal/cloneplan/nullability_test.go:120 toggles byte_count, blob_id, and blob_descriptor_id together. TestEntryBranchLiterals covers each missing alone, leaving two-missing combinations unmeasured. The branchcombo-plant.patch bypasses the guard for one such combination; BuildProjectedObjectManifest then dereferences nil.\",\n103|      \"reproductions\": [\n104|        {\n105|          \"test_file\": \"review_branchcombo_test.go\",\n106|          \"command\": \"go test -count=1 -run '^TestReviewBlobDoubleMissingRefusal$' ./internal/cloneplan on exact candidate: exit 0\",\n107|          \"expected_failure\": \"on branchcombo-plant.patch: expected test failure through a panic, exit 1; logs branchcombo-candidate.log and branchcombo-branchcombo.log\",\n108|          \"pinned_blobs\": [\n109|            \"sha256:041984a72c5e9cd8b59dfb533ffe2e56733370e3f15b0299f00e2de634dddfa3\",\n110|            \"sha256:64ee2403895a0b12fcbd22b377ba9a82a8c46748f35b53fcf0701f351f5a1082\"\n111|          ]\n112|        },\n113|        {\n114|          \"test_file\": \"go test -count=1 ./internal/cloneplan on the branchcombo mutant without the review test: exit 0\",\n115|          \"command\": \"log branchcombo-existing-suite.log\",\n116|          \"expected_failure\": \"go test -count=1 ./internal/cloneplan on the branchcombo mutant without the review test: exit 0; log branchcombo-existing-suite.log\",\n117|          \"pinned_blobs\": [\n118|            \"sha256:041984a72c5e9cd8b59dfb533ffe2e56733370e3f15b0299f00e2de634dddfa3\",\n119|            \"sha256:64ee2403895a0b12fcbd22b377ba9a82a8c46748f35b53fcf0701f351f5a1082\"\n120|          ]\n121|        },\n122|        {\n123|          \"test_file\": \"coverage_audit.py <exact candidate copy>: expected exit 1 for the absent independent three-field grid\",\n124|          \"command\": \"log coverage-audit.log\",\n125|          \"expected_failure\": \"coverage_audit.py <exact candidate copy>: expected exit 1 for the absent independent three-field grid; log coverage-audit.log\",\n126|          \"pinned_blobs\": [\n127|            \"sha256:041984a72c5e9cd8b59dfb533ffe2e56733370e3f15b0299f00e2de634dddfa3\",\n128|            \"sha256:64ee2403895a0b12fcbd22b377ba9a82a8c46748f35b53fcf0701f351f5a1082\"\n129|          ]\n130|        }\n131|      ],\n132|      \"severity\": \"robustness\",\n133|      \"repeat-of\": \"none\"\n134|    },\n135|    {\n136|      \"id\": \"exact-tree-diff-check-missed\",\n137|      \"row\": \"Exact-tree hygiene\",\n138|      \"invariant\": \"The candidate passes the required lint/diff hygiene check on the reviewable tree, and the reported validation covers that same tree.\",\n139|      \"mechanism\": \"internal/cloneplan/testdata/mutant_harness.py:1325 adds a blank line at EOF. The CR validation log ran plain git diff --check against an untracked-only package, which produced exit 0 without checking those files.\",\n140|      \"reproductions\": [\n141|        {\n142|          \"test_file\": \"diff-check\",\n143|          \"command\": \"git diff --check 547ea289e411bea803f4cd47b6314e4bb558ceb0 c4fbfc7922287a2abfaadedbb37eba93308b1cdc on exact candidate blobs: expected failure exit 2, new blank line at EOF\",\n144|          \"expected_failure\": \"compare CR validation log's plain git diff --check exit 0\",\n145|          \"pinned_blobs\": [\n146|            \"sha256:7cb3be7525b463b25cf427048aaeef3a4d79f01f36b6adec64c3cd88b988dc30\"\n147|          ]\n148|        }\n149|      ],\n150|      \"severity\": \"regression\",\n151|      \"repeat-of\": \"none\"\n152|    }\n153|  ],\n154|  \"notes\": [\n155|    \"The case-only unknownMember plant survived because a separate missing-member gate still refused; it is not a finding.\",\n156|    \"The importer table lacks explicit (package, entry, input) keys; six owner packages are byte-identical and their base/candidate tests passed, so no moved class was found.\",\n157|    \"The 1,000,000 mapping upper edge is checked at a helper, not a public entry; it remains an unchecked edge of AC row 16.\"\n158|  ],\n159|  \"surface_results\": [\n160|    {\n161|      \"row\": \"Closed member sets and strict frame\",\n162|      \"result\": \"broken\"\n163|    },\n164|    {\n165|      \"row\": \"Operation ordering and DAG\",\n166|      \"result\": \"broken\"\n167|    },\n168|    {\n169|      \"row\": \"Resource and entry nullability\",\n170|      \"result\": \"broken\"\n171|    },\n172|    {\n173|      \"row\": \"Sorted arrays, scalar bounds, plan constants, policies, vocabulary\",\n174|      \"result\": \"held\"\n175|    },\n176|    {\n177|      \"row\": \"Omit-self JCS identities\",\n178|      \"result\": \"held\"\n179|    },\n180|    {\n181|      \"row\": \"Importer outcomes and composition\",\n182|      \"result\": \"held\"\n183|    },\n184|    {\n185|      \"row\": \"Exact-tree hygiene\",\n186|      \"result\": \"broken\"\n187|    }\n188|  ],\n189|  \"free_hunt\": []\n190|}\n191|```\n192|\n193|## Notes\n194|\n195|- The case-only `unknownMember` plant in `own_plants.py` survived because the independent missing-member gate still refused the document. It was dropped as a non-finding; `case_member.log` records this.\n196|- The producer's importer table is not keyed by `(package, entry, input)`. My byte-identity comparison and base/candidate package runs found no moved class, so this formatting gap did not become a separate blocking finding.\n197|- The mapping upper count of 1,000,000 is tested at `checkMappingCount` in `counts_internal_test.go`, but not sealed/decoded at the production entries. This is an unchecked edge of AC row 16 and should be closed or reported as an explicit entry-level bound in the next revision.\n198|- The producer's claimed 18/18 leaf rows counts rows 1, 5, 14, and 16 as fully driven. My measured complete production-entry coverage is **14 of 18 AC rows**. The rest have named tests but lack the requested derived census, whole graph/domain grid, or entry-level upper edge. Planning semantics belong to TASK-260924-3n78rv and are excluded from this denominator.\n199|- No baseline production bypass was found in the attacked inputs. The three surviving plants show that the submitted tests permit distinct weakenings; they are not claims that the exact candidate currently admits those inputs.\n200|\n201|## Validation and rework scope (for the producer)\n202|\n203|The exact tree passed `go test -count=1 ./...`, `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go vet ./...`, `go test -count=3 ./internal/cloneplan/...`, and independent JCS recomputation for the plan and manifest fixtures. Base and candidate reused-owner package tests passed, with byte-identical code. The shipped 117 narrowing plants and one applied harmless control were rerun twice by this reviewer; see the two run summaries and per-plant logs in the evidence tar. `gofmt -l` returned no Go files. The exact-tree `git diff --check` failed as above.\n204|\n205|Add a reflection-derived member census covering all schema types and multiple miscasing forms; commit the titlecase refusal test. Enumerate invalid as well as valid four/five-operation dependency graphs or provide an equivalent generated whole-domain proof that kills the four-node self-edge plant. Sweep all independent blob-only member-presence combinations through Build and Decode with structured-refusal assertions and kill the two-missing plant. Close or explicitly bound the million-mapping production-entry edge, expand the importer table to the requested triple key, remove the blank line, and run diff hygiene against the snapshotted candidate rather than the live untracked diff. Update the measured coverage ratio and conformance matrix from the resulting tests. Reuse this same task/CR rework path; no separate research or architecture decision is needed.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260924-3n78rv/TASK-260924-3n78rv_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--muse-_RUN-260924-aa8f5f.log:891:{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000ca3d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0d24d-9c2d-7841-a066-6ac00d915ab7"},"sequence":889,"recorded_at":1780531400001773,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"6722cf1c-e919-40c8-89ba-6768c67dec7c","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"6722cf1c-e919-40c8-89ba-6768c67dec7c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"6722cf1c-e919-40c8-89ba-6768c67dec7c"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0d250-848d-7201-a0f3-63ab17bbaf85"},"task_id":"01a0d250-848d-7201-a0f3-63ab17bbaf85","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0d250-848d-7201-a0f3-63ab17bbaf85","chunk":"Read text file `.temp/TASK-260924-3n78rv/jmmqn-results.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-1jmmqn results: projection-plan schemas (rework rev4)\n2|\n3|Candidate: UNCOMMITTED tree in the STORY-260830-21bxa3 worktree.\n4|Scope: `internal/cloneplan` (new files only; no landed file edited,\n5|no registry edit). Change Request is `task_delta`. Base trunk\n6|`0ca3e4c` is an ancestor of the checkpoint (`git merge-base\n7|--is-ancestor 0ca3e4c HEAD` exits 0; HEAD `547ea28`): no refresh\n8|needed.\n9|\n10|This revision answers the rev3 finding\n11|(`plan-constant-second-value-uncounted`). Every rev1 finding stays\n12|closed; every rev1 production line is intact (plans.go still\n13|`sha256:c2f7eb93506291635218beb49a589d8920bf32459d2906d73c9c3c74e311f02f`,\n14|the reviewer's pinned blob). The diff is tests + harness +\n15|TRACEABILITY, plus one new test file\n16|(`constants_closed_test.go`).\n17|\n18|## What changed per the finding\n19|\n20|The rev3 finding: `TestPlanConstants` probed three invalid\n21|`materialization_intent` strings (`prepare`, `clone2`, `Clone`),\n22|so a gate widened to admit `copy` survived the submitted suite on\n23|both sides. The invalid domain of a closed constant is every other\n24|string, which is unbounded; this revision closes it BY\n25|CONSTRUCTION, exactly per the rework brief:\n26|\n27|1. Named regression (`TestPlanConstantCopyRegression`): `copy`\n28|   refuses at every closed string gate (4 nested constants +\n29|   modes + 4 schema/version literals) on both entries, 14\n30|   subtests, literal refusal tokens. Each subtest carries sibling\n31|   probes (the literal admits, the first derived neighbor\n32|   refuses), so the kill lands on the `copy-refuses` probe only.\n33|2. Generated invalid values (`TestPlanConstantGeneratedSweep`,\n34|   `TestPlanConstantDerivedValues`, `TestPlanConstantBooleans`,\n35|   `TestPlanConstantNonBooleanJSON`): per string literal at both\n36|   entries, every edit-distance-1 neighbor over\n37|   lowercase+digit+`_`, every case variant class (reusing the\n38|   census `caseVariantsOf`), a fixed-seed 200-string sample, the\n39|   `copy` probe, empty, whitespace paddings, and the 5-value\n40|   non-string JSON grid at decode; per boolean, the other boolean\n41|   both entries plus all 5 non-boolean JSON types at decode;\n42|   modes adds per-element neighbor/case sweeps, the order swap,\n43|   lengths 0..4, non-string elements, and non-array JSON. The\n44|   whole sweep runs in ~2s.\n45|3. Structural guard (`TestClosedConstantGateShape`): the gate\n46|   LIST derives mechanically (reflection over the four nested\n47|   plan input types, maps skipped by kind; build/decode functions\n48|   found by type signature; the modes checker found by call\n49|   shape), cross-checked both directions against the spec oracle\n50|   (SPEC.v0.7.0.md:10703-10718, 10654, 168-169). Each gate must\n51|   be one equality against the oracle literal; the\n52|   comparison-literal set per file must equal the oracle set\n53|   exactly; no switch, no prefix/fold/contains/normalize call.\n54|   Control plants: the reviewer's build-side copy widening\n55|   reddens it (exit 1), a two-case switch reddens it (exit 1),\n56|   and a bonus decode-side copy widening reddens it (exit 1);\n57|   pristine passes (exit 0). Production restored byte-identical\n58|   after each plant (sha re-verified).\n59|4. Mutants: 13 copy-admitting narrowings (`N-copy-*`, one per\n60|   string gate per side plus the shared modes gate and the 4\n61|   decode-only schema/version literals) killed by the named\n62|   copy-regression subtests ALONE, and 7 null-admitting decode\n63|   narrowings (`N-null-*`, one per closed boolean gate) killed by\n64|   the named non-boolean subtests ALONE. Battery is now 145 rows:\n65|   143 narrowing + 1 marked arm-delete + 1 neutral control\n66|   SURVIVED.\n67|\n68|## AC coverage, measured: 18 of 18 leaf-schema rows driven\n69|\n70|Denominator: the 18 leaf-schema rows (planning semantics excluded\n71|per the orchestrator split). Each row names its production call\n72|site; every refusal below is literal-pinned and every gate carries\n73|a killed narrowing (matrix names them). Rows 8-11 are now carried\n74|by the construction above; all other rows unchanged from rev2.\n75|\n76|| # | Row | Call site | Test |\n77||---|---|---|---|\n78|| 1 | Plan 36-member set + schema/version literals | D | Derived census + UnknownMissing + Miscased(6 classes) + WrongTypes + Duplicated(every member) + NoLiteralList + SchemaLiterals + CopyRegression + DerivedValues + GeneratedSweep + GateShape |\n79|| 2 | `projection_plan_id` omit-self identity | B, D | TestPlanIdentityIndependent |\n80|| 3 | Mapping shape + disposition/reason vocabs | B, D | Census + ExpectedDisposition/MappingReason oracles |\n81|| 4 | Operation shape + sequence order | B, D | Census + DAGRefusalLiterals |\n82|| 5 | Dependency DAG vs oracle | B, D (shared gate) | WholeDomainCensus + ValidFive + Locality + SingleEdge + RefusalLiterals |\n83|| 6 | Resource branch-exact nullability | B, D (shared gate) | ResourceNullabilityGrid (12/12 full) + BranchLiterals |\n84|| 7 | Synth event shape + purposes | B, D | Census + SynthesizedPurposeOracle |\n85|| 8-11 | Transaction/ReadBack/Resume/Rollback constants | B, D | TestPlanConstants + CopyRegression + DerivedValues + GeneratedSweep + Booleans + NonBooleanJSON + GateShape |\n86|| 12 | ContractRequirement (id, SemVer, no ext) | B, D | TestContractSemver + TestContractNoExtensions |\n87|| 13 | Manifest 10-member set + identity | MB, MD | Derived census + SchemaLiterals + ManifestIdentityIndependent + CopyRegression + DerivedValues + GeneratedSweep + GateShape |\n88|| 14 | Entry branch-exact member sets | MB, MD | EntryNullabilityGrid (48/48 full) + GridNeverPanics + EntryBranchLiterals |\n89|| 15 | Sorting/uniqueness on every ordered array | B, D, MB, MD | TestSortedUniqueSweep + TestRowOrderSweep |\n90|| 16 | Every bound at edge and edge+1 | B, D, MB, MD | CountEdges + MillionEntryLevel + FactoredCountGates + String/Number edges |\n91|| 17 | Policy maps | B, D | TestRequiredDispositions + TestSecurityExclusions |\n92|| 18 | Scalar delegation | B, D, MB, MD | TestScalarGates + TestManifestScalarGates + TestNumberModel |\n93|\n94|Stated bounds (not waived): the unbounded remainder past the\n95|generated invalid set is closed by the structural guard (any\n96|second value changes the gate shape or the comparison-literal\n97|set), not by sampling; 5-op DAG coverage is structural (33M\n98|graphs infeasible); the literal-list guard trips at census scale\n99|(10+/40%+); JSON-level member probes run at decode entries while\n100|build runs the per-field zero census. Cross-artifact couplings,\n101|`total_bytes` derivation, and synthesized order stay bounded as in\n102|rev1 (TRACEABILITY).\n103|\n104|## Out-of-contract rows (declared, not silent)\n105|\n106|- \"Plan pair-neutral target projection, checkpoint message\n107|  authority, inactive tools/instructions, token metadata, and\n108|  vendor importer strategies\" as PLANNING SEMANTICS: sibling leaf\n109|  TASK-260924-3n78rv (or